# @MT:XL
Nordshrift .sst Scripting Sheet Format Specification

.sst Format Reference — Normative Edition

Document Series:	NS-SST-0001
Document Status:	Normative
Revision:	1.0.0
Date:	September 2026
Governing Tool:	Nordshrift Transpiler Driver, version 1.0
Companion Document:	Sleela Language Metadocument SL-META-0001
Preamble
Purpose
Nordshrift is the transpiler driver for the Sleela programming language. It reads one or more .sst (Scripting Sheet) files and uses them to configure, drive, and extend every phase of the Sleela-to-Java transpilation pipeline defined in SL-META-0001, Chapter 6. A .sst file is the primary human-authored control surface for Nordshrift: it specifies source inputs, transformation targets, pipeline phase configuration, rule activation, effect policies, derivation instructions, Java interoperability settings, and named compilation profiles.

Scope
This document specifies:

The lexical conventions of the .sst format
The complete block and section grammar
Every directive, its syntax, its operands, and its semantics
Import and composition rules
Profile resolution and override mechanics
All Nordshrift-specific error codes and their triggering conditions
The relationship between .sst constructs and Sleela meta-model concepts
Normative Status
All statements in this document using must, must not, shall, shall not, required, and forbidden are normative. Statements using should, may, recommended, and optional are non-normative guidance.

Relationship to SL-META-0001
The .sst format is explicitly subordinate to the Sleela Language Metadocument. Where this document refers to Sleela meta-model concepts — Entity, Contract, Effect, Rule, Lens, Context, Flow, Projection — those terms carry the definitions from SL-META-0001 §2.2. Where this document specifies compilation pipeline phases, phase numbering and naming follow SL-META-0001 §6.1.

