Appendix D — Relationship to SL-META-0001
.sst Section	SL-META Concept	SL-META Chapter / Phase	Notes
source	Source Input Set	Chapter 6, Phase 1	Configures the file set fed to Lexical Analysis.
target	Java Emission Surface	§3.4; Phases 10–11	Implements Idiomatic Java and Deterministic Output guarantees.
pipeline	Compilation Pipeline	§6.1; Phases 1–11	Maps tokens directly to SL-META phase numbers and names.
rules	Rule primitive	§2.2; Phase 7	Activates and configures Rule evaluation at Phase 7.
effects	Effect primitive	§2.2; Phase 6	Declares the Effect vocabulary and configures Phase 6 policy.
derive	Derive Blocks	§3.3	Controls derivation of Lenses, Projections, and structural methods from Entities.
guards	Guard Clauses	§3.3	Configures compile-time and runtime enforcement of Flow preconditions and postconditions.
interop	Java Interoperability Boundary	§7.4	Governs effect assignment, null wrapping, and type mapping at the Java call boundary.
profile	(no direct meta-model concept)	§6.1 (invocation)	Nordshrift-level mechanism for named build variant configuration; no Sleela meta-model counterpart.
sheet	(no direct meta-model concept)	—	File-level manifest; provides identity and versioning metadata for the .sst file itself.
import	(no direct meta-model concept)	—	Composition mechanism for .sst files; analogous to module imports in Sleela source but distinct.
rule (inline block)	Rule primitive	§2.2; Phase 7	Per-rule configuration block; fine-grained override of rules: section entries.
